+  \begin{itemize}
+    \item Motifs recur across cortical layers
+    \item Non-uniform influence: hubs dominate output
+    \item Specificity differs by cell class
+  \end{itemize}
+  \vspace{2mm}
+  \colorbox{gold!22!bg}{\parbox{0.95\linewidth}{\fontsize{30}{38}\selectfont\color{text}\textbf{Design rule:} sparse hubs + modular motifs \;$\to$\; robust computation.}}
+  \vspace{2mm}
+  \colorbox{teal!20!bg}{\parbox{0.95\linewidth}{\fontsize{30}{38}\selectfont\color{text}\textbf{Layer logic:} feedforward streams + recurrent integrators.}}
+  }
+}
+
+\posterbox[tealcard]{name=implications, column=3, between=row11 and row16}{%
+  {\fontsize{34}{44}\selectfont\color{text}
+  \textbf{Implications \& Next Steps}}\\[2mm]
+  \begin{itemize}
+    \item Motif “vocabulary” \;$\to$\; compositional models of cortex
+    \item Hubs explain widespread effects of focal perturbations
+    \item Better priors for disease, stimulation, BCI design
+  \end{itemize}
+  \vspace{2mm}
+  \colorbox{teal!22!bg}{\parbox{0.95\linewidth}{\fontsize{30}{38}\selectfont\color{text}\textbf{Next:} extend to regions, species, whole-brain wiring.}}
+  \vspace{2mm}
